Optional raylib: CMake option PS2X_WITH_RAYLIB (default ON); OFF builds the runtime library with no raylib

What it fixes: the runtime library always fetched, compiled and linked raylib (plus imgui and rlImGui for
the debug UI), even for a host that owns its window, audio and input (patches 0007 and 0008) and never
uses them; a host linking SDL3 would carry two window systems. With -DPS2X_WITH_RAYLIB=OFF:

  ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt   FetchContent of raylib, imgui and rlImGui is skipped (nothing is fetched);
        ps2_host_backend links nothing and defines PS2X_NO_RAYLIB for everything that links ps2_runtime;
        the ps2EntryRunner executable (raylib window, debug UI, src/main.cpp) is not built or installed.
        The ps2_runtime include directories and link line moved up, out of the runner section, unchanged.
  ps2_host_backend.h            includes raylib.h only without PS2X_NO_RAYLIB.
  raylib call sites with PS2X_NO_RAYLIB:
    ps2_runtime.cpp  UploadFrame (UpdateTexture) compiled out; initialize() without setHostOwnsWindow(true)
        prints "[don] this build of the runtime has no window of its own ..." and returns false; run()
        without it prints the same and returns (with it, run() is the waiting loop of patch 0007); the
        destructor's CloseAudioDevice/CloseWindow compiled out;
    ps2_pad.cpp, ps2_pad.h  readRaylibState compiled out, PSPadBackend::hostMode() is always true: input
        comes only from the host source of patch 0008, none installed means not connected;
    Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp  applyGamepadState / applyKeyboardState / findFirstGamepad / axisToByte and the
        PS2_IF_AGRESSIVE_LOGS keyboard trace compiled out (empty replacements);
    ps2_audio.cpp  the raylib Sound code (playDecodedSample, pruneFinishedSounds, stopAll) is compiled out
        the same way as on the Vita; the host's SPU2 (patch 0006) is then the only sound path;
    ps2_debug_panel.cpp and src/main.cpp are only part of ps2EntryRunner and are not built.
  Nothing else of the library included raylib: no further change was needed.
With the option ON (the default) nothing changes in what is built or fetched.

How it was verified: a second build tree configured with -DPS2X_WITH_RAYLIB=OFF and
-DFETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED=ON and no raylib/imgui source directories: the configure step succeeds
and creates no _deps directory (nothing fetched); libps2_runtime.a has no symbol matching raylib, imgui or
rlImGui (nm); host_loop_test and host_pad_source_test build against it and pass with DISPLAY unset
(vsyncs at 60.00 Hz, pads from the host source, initialize() without the host flag fails loudly). The same
tests built with raylib (option ON) pass as before. Not exercised: building ps2EntryRunner (needs raylib and
a display to run), Windows and the Vita/Android paths.

Based on: original work for this project against PS2Recomp commit
2c5fbb9389e11dd95693385969490c9e8e6f57b4, on top of patches 0001 to 0006, 0007 and 0008.

